<title>SINGAPORE: ST Capital 1996 net profit up 15.1 pct.</title>
<headline>ST Capital 1996 net profit up 15.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			 19.32     vs    16.79</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)	    13.50     vs    11.70</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)	     25.00     vs    25.00</p>
<p>    Special dividend (pct)	  5.00     vs     nil</p>
<p>    Interest income		  46.94     vs    39.18</p>
<p>    Interest expense		 22.95     vs    16.50</p>
<p>    Income from int.rate swaps    2.23     vs     2.64</p>
<p>    Operating lease income	 37.86     vs    31.49</p>
<p>    Depreciation		     22.76     vs    17.68</p>
<p>    Other income			5.43     vs     5.05</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		   25.03     vs    22.21</p>
<p>    Tax				   5.71     vs     5.42</p>
<p>    Dividend register/pay date:   June 24, 1997/July 3, 1997</p>
<p>Note - ST Capital Ltd is a unit of Singapore Technologies Industrial Corp.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
